What:           /dev/stpbt
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        AIC A1260 bring-up maintainers
Description:
                Exclusive H4 byte stream for the MT6580 STP BT task. Opening
                takes the Bluetooth WMT function vote; closing releases only
                that vote, preserving a concurrent Wi-Fi owner. A second open
                returns EBUSY. This is not a Linux hci_uart or AF_BLUETOOTH
                interface. Userspace supplies calibration and HCI initialization.

                Reads support blocking, O_NONBLOCK and poll. An empty nonblocking
                read returns EAGAIN. Writes are limited to 4096 bytes and return
                EAGAIN when STP has no credit. Poll writability is advisory;
                callers must handle EAGAIN. A WMT reset faults the open stream:
                reads/writes return EIO and poll reports ERR/HUP. Close/reopen
                and controller initialization are required after such a reset.
                Legacy vendor ioctls and in-kernel NVRAM file I/O are absent.

What:           /sys/class/misc/stpbt/state
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        AIC A1260 bring-up maintainers
Description:
                Read-only cached counters, without MMIO or a power transition:
                opened, fault, opens, closes, rx, tx and events. rx/tx are
                successfully delivered byte counts; events counts STP receive
                notifications. Counters are cumulative since driver startup.
                opened also includes an in-progress open; fault is cleared on
                the next exclusive open. A receive notification issues a bounded
                250ms wakeup event rather than holding a permanent wake lock.
